# ===========================================
# Quizify — HACS-ready repo
# ===========================================

# ---- Dev / build frameworks ----
.claude/*
# …except the stats skill. The report it produces is quoted in the chat and in
# the wiki, and two bugs in it shipped unnoticed because the file was invisible
# to every diff. Only this one skill is un-ignored; logs and the other skills
# stay out.
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/quizify-stats/
docs/*
# docs/ holds local working material (design shotguns, scratch), but the
# release notes are a published artefact: they are the prose behind each
# GitHub release and the only place that history is readable in the repo.
# Keeping them ignored is why the directory sat with a single stale file.
#
# The pattern must be ``docs/*``, not ``docs/``: git does not descend into an
# excluded *directory*, so a negation below it never gets evaluated. With
# ``docs/`` the rule below looked right and did nothing — every new release
# notes file stayed invisible to ``git add`` and only landed if someone
# happened to force-add it (which is how v1.4–v1.6 got in, and how v1.7.0
# nearly did not).
!docs/release-notes/
.playwright-mcp/

# ---- Config & tooling ----
# pyproject.toml IS tracked: it holds the ruff lint-gate config the CI
# `ruff check` job relies on (issues #306/#328). Without it committed the
# gate would silently fall back to ruff's defaults.
package.json
package-lock.json
requirements.txt
.ruff.toml

# ---- Tests ----
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# ---- Node ----
node_modules/

# ---- Python artifacts ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
eggs/
.eggs/

# ---- Linting ----
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---- IDE ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Misc ----
*.bak
.gstack/

# ---- Standalone dev server state (scripts/dev_server.py) ----
.quizify-data/

# ---- Local QA venv ----
.qa-venv/
